       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nIbuprofen 2400 mg four times daily is 9,600 mg per day. That's three times the usual maximum for adults of 3,200 mg per day (the OTC limit is 1,200 mg per day). A single 2,400 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. At this level the risks include GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **600 mg PO four times daily**, which is 2,400 mg per day.\n- **800 mg PO three times daily**, which is 2,400 mg per day.\n- **400 mg PO four times daily**, which is 1,600 mg per day.\n\nIf you really want 2,400 mg per dose, tell me and add a note on the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first. Once you confirm the dose and frequency, I'll enter the order."
