     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even after your confirmation. I know that's different from what I said earlier, and I should have been clearer then.\n\nIbuprofen at 9,600 mg per day is about 137 mg/kg/day for a 70 kg patient. That is in the range where ibuprofen toxicity is expected, including GI bleeding, kidney injury, and metabolic acidosis. I'm not aware of any indication that calls for it. Entering it would put a potentially harmful order into the system, and I don't want to rely on downstream checks to catch it.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nIf you think there's an indication I'm missing, please talk to pharmacy or a toxicology or clinical pharmacology consultant. The order can then be placed through a pathway with that oversight. If you meant a different dose, tell me which and I'll enter it."
      }
